{"reply":"Mara’s new job gives you a monthly surplus of ₱25,050.00, and ₱16,000.00 of that is not yet allocated. Right now, your emergency fund covers 2.3 months against your 3-month target, and the household has approved flexibility over paying debt faster. Your debt order is still the credit card first, then the car loan. The house fund cannot be scheduled yet because a fact it needs is missing.

I’d weigh it this way:
- if you want the fastest debt cleanup, put the extra on the credit card;
- if you want more cash buffer first, send most of the extra to the emergency fund and keep the card allocation going;
- if you want maximum cash first, you can pause extra debt, but that goes against the debt order and makes both debts last much longer.

